# The oracle corpus is byte-addressed, so it must never be line-ending converted.
#
# fixtures/MANIFEST.sha256 records the sha256 of every file under fixtures/, and the Swift
# FixturesManifestTests in HarmonizerMobile recomputes all of them. The repo is checked out with
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on a Windows checkout - that would silently break
# every one of the 1,350 hashes, and the .jsonl traces and .f32 payloads are compared by hash too.
#
# `-text` means "do no end-of-line conversion": the bytes in the blob are the bytes on disk, on
# every platform. This is what makes the corpus portable, and it is why the goldens are written
# with an explicit newline="\n" by the Python tooling.
fixtures/** -text
